          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For a dry, undamaged garage with ordinary traffic and an owner willing to prepare the slab properly, EpoxyShield is a sound choice. It is easy to apply, reasonably priced and widely available, and it gives a clean, easy-to-maintain floor. It is thin, though, and it rewards good prep and punishes shortcuts.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Grind the floor, buy a spare kit, add a UV-resistant topcoat with anti-slip additive, and wait the full cure before parking. Do that, and EpoxyShield should serve you well for several years. If you need more durability or speed, step up to RockSolid or a thick-build system instead.
          </p>
